WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.767
New overnight.

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.768
Ukrainian military

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.570
says it has inflicted huge

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.572
losses on Russian forces

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:06.573
in what they call

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.341
a successful counterattack

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.276
near the eastern city. Of Bakhmut.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.678
This is where so much fighting

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:12.379
has taken place

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:13.947
over the last several months.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:15.515
The leader of the volunteer group,

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.783
which is a Russian backed

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.785
mercenary organization fighting there,

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:19.386
is now

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.387
also accusing

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:22.956
Russian regular troops of fleeing.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.091
With us now is CNN military

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.126
analyst, retired Major

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.360
General James Spider Marks.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.995
General, great to see you here.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:29.896
John,
this fighting

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.698
back about this counter attack

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:32.432
that Ukrainians

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.700
are claiming some success in

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.268
to see the leader of Bognor

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.037
maybe verify that.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.438
Describe the significance.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.407
Well,
what's probably happening right now is

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.141
the Ukrainians

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.475
are having some great success

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.743
of removing what we call

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:44.244
the enemy's

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:46.413
eyes, their ability to do reconnaissance

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.214
against the Ukrainians,

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.582
Ukrainians are then conducting

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:50.850
counter reconnaissance,

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.452
deciding where they want to attack,

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:53.720
which is what we've demonstrated

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.655
right in here, where they want to attack.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:56.990
So they concentrate fire.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.825
They concentrate forces

00:00:58.825 --> 00:00:59.793
and then they penetrate

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.094
through a salient as quickly

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:03.029
and as deeply as they can.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.331
Well, that that maneuver takes

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:06.599
time, takes a lot of effort.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:07.567
We've seen the build up

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.869
or we've anticipated the buildup.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.072
The Wagner forces probably have realized

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.506
they were at the tip of the spear.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.441
We're not deep enough.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.009
We're not fulsome enough.

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.310
And the Ukrainian forces

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.612
have stripped them away.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.847
And so that's the challenge

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:21.781
that they're seeing right now.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:22.082
All right.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:22.816
So I'm going to reset

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:23.616
and put it back up again.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:24.284
That's a battle.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.185
What we're seeing

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:26.653
is a battle

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.088
what we have been expecting

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.222
for some time.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.324
Deals in the war, this counteroffensive.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.860
Show me where that could take place

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.828
and how this plays out,

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:35.762
John, is the difference

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.297
between tactical success

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.032
and operational victories?

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.500
You have to tie together

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.735
a number of tactical engagements,

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.804
which the Ukrainians do magnificently.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:45.572
They've demonstrated

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.307
creativity, innovation,

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.875
fearlessness in combat.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.610
But you have to have the heft.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.912
You have to have the mass, the amount,

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.547
the volume of forces

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.549
to tie tactical victories together

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.951
here and here

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:59.586
and then you achieve this penetration.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.621
Then you can hold on one side

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.156
and then you can reduce

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.224
in that direction.

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:05.525
We haven't seen that yet.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.694
So we are seeing the start of

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:08.728
tactical victories

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:09.796
that then need to lead

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.632
to some type of operational advantage.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.801
Let me put a different map up in

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:15.602
I'm going to Mark

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.536
where you just had before.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.004
This is where you've seen

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:18.938
the fighting there

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.540
and tell people that there have been

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.008
Ukrainian drone

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.210
strikes in Russian territory

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.146
here, here, here.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.347
And then in previous weeks,

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:28.481
we've seen some attacks here

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.518
and also in Russian occupied Crimea.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.953
So this is what the Ukrainians are

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.021
said to be doing.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:37.223
How are these drone attacks important?

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.192
Perhaps to the counter offensive?

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.527
Hugely important.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.895
It's about time

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.364
Russians in this area have sanctuary.

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.933
They can go back, they can refit,

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.234
they can reorganize,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.670
they can rest, they can refuel, etc.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.339
So they prepare for engagements.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.774
When you are in sanctuary,

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.176
that gives you all the advantage.

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:58.411
When you have no ability to rest,

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.146
you have no ability to refuel

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:00.947
and you're back here

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.315
and you're being attacked,

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.217
that reduces your ability

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.252
to concentrate forces going forward.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.621
So these are the deep fires

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.923
that are essential

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.991
to achieve that operational maneuver.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:12.759
If the

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.260
if the Ukrainians can continue

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.429
to apply pressure across the border

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.164
into the sanctuary areas

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:19.732
where the Russian forces are.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:20.333
It will limit

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.501
the number of Russian forces.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.769
It'll give the advantage

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:23.836
to the Ukrainians

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.471
to achieve that level of success.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.039
It may be

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.274
that we are seeing signs of coordination.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.643
Yes. About what is to come.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:31.911
This is synchronization

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:32.845
that we probably haven't

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.747
seen at this level yet.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:35.648
This is good news.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:36.983
Retired General James Spider Marks

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.051
always a pleasure to see you.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.285
Even better in person. Thanks.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.353
So thank you, John.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.088
The governors of three border regions say

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:44.290
they were attacked by Ukrainian drones

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.158
claiming the targets

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.627
included a military facility

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.462
Meanwhile, the Ukrainian military says

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.064
it's inflicted, quote, huge

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.299
losses on Russian forces

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.867
near the city of buck moot.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.003
Nick Paton Walsh joins us now

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.004
Nick, good to have you with us.

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.439
And so many echoes

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:00.873
the complaints that we got last week

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:01.441
once again

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.208
from the Russians chief

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.309
saying that they were in dire

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.411
need of weaponry, reinforcements.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.479
Do we have any way to

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.414
verify the Ukrainian claims

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.085
Well, partly because

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:12.919
they're echoed indeed

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:13.786
by Faulkner

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.655
themselves, who initially brought

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.156
to attention

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:17.724
the belief

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:19.926
that a certain part

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:22.161
of the southern front around back moves.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.297
There'd been a three kilometer

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:25.298
deep retreat

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.467
by some parts of the Russian military,

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.502
the 72nd mechanized brigade

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:30.570
was the initial claim.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.371
Now, that was first aired

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:31.904
by Yevgeny

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.373
Prigozhin, the former head, saying

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:34.574
that he'd lost 500 men

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:35.875
fighting for that area.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:36.676
And again,

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:39.512
he used this example as another moment to

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:40.413
to poke

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.181
at the Russian conventional military,

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.449
saying that it was the Russian

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.517
conventional troops

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.952
who departed this area

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.520
and essentially casting Wagner

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.289
as those doing the bulk of the serious

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.823
fighting to hang on to bulk.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:53.660
But it's another display of disunity here

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.261
and also an example

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.297
that the fighting around back

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:59.599
is definitely not going in Russia's way.

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:00.733
A stark reversal

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.168
from a matter of weeks ago

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:04.037
where we persistently heard thoughts

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:05.004
that perhaps Russia

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.439
might have the upper hand,

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:07.173
might be able

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.075
to potentially close off

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:09.909
and encircle

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.678
the remaining Ukrainian troops in there.

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:14.280
Now, we've had a week of public comments

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.381
from Evgeny Prigozhin

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.417
saying he would leave today entirely

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:18.251
because he didn't have enough

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.352
artillery shells,

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.087
then saying he would stay,

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:21.721
then saying

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.989
he actually wasn't getting enough

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.258
and now blaming the Russian army itself

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:26.192
for pulling away

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:27.460
from a key part of the front.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.461
None of this is good

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.897
for Russian morale or frankly,

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:31.964
for the grip of Vladimir

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.766
Putin on this increasingly

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:34.834
disastrous war.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.035
We are days away,

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.537
if not already, in the early stages

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.138
of Ukrainian counteroffensive.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:39.739
And so

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:41.207
Russian troops in the trenches

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:43.242
are hearing their most probably prominent

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.477
Russian military figure.

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:46.012
Prigozhin speak

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.847
very disparagingly about the command

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.716
as a top brass running this war.

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:50.450
And indeed, now

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.684
this appears to be translating

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:52.985
into a small

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.120
but significant

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.888
still the deeply symbolic

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:57.256
collapse of Russian positions

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.124
along this front line

00:05:58.124 --> 00:06:00.426
confirmed by Ukrainian military officials

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.260
who said, in fact,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.329
their troops managed to push forward.

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:05.231
So we're seeing a lot changing here

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:06.499
around back moves.

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:07.934
So symbolic for Russia.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:09.702
The one thing they said they would take,

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.070
they said they take it by today,

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.672
finally, that hasn't happened.

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:13.373
And instead,

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:14.374
we're seeing parts

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:15.274
of the Russian military,

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:16.476
it seems eroding small,

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:19.078
but still potentially important positions

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:20.079
around that city.

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:22.148
Julia, I can only imagine what impact

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:23.349
this is having on morale.

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:24.050
Nick, what

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.351
can you tell us about

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:26.152
the Ukrainian saying

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:28.020
that Russia won't allow staff

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.088
of the separation

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.324
power plant, the nuclear power plant,

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:33.326
of course, to evacuate the nearby town?

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:34.494
Absolutely.

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:36.829
On the front lines of any apparent

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:39.866
started or impending counterattack by

00:06:39.866 --> 00:06:40.600
the Ukrainians,

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:43.503
Yeah.
Look, I

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:43.936
mean, it's

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:45.505
unclear exactly what's happening

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:47.573
inside as average a nuclear power plant.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:50.810
It has been held up so often by Russian

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.779
occupying forces are sort of elements

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:54.013
of nuclear blackmail.

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:55.882
And we don't really know quite

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:56.949
what is happening

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.351
inside it all around it.

00:06:58.351 --> 00:07:00.653
We do know that in that region,

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:01.854
there's been

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:04.257
evacuations called by the Russian

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.792
occupying forces.

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:08.060
3000 of the last figure of civilians,

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:08.828
they said they moved away

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:10.630
from frontline towns.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.698
Certainly that includes the areas,

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:13.866
large numbers around

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:16.302
potentially the Aparicio plan, that town

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.271
being evacuated and their goddaughter.

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:19.138
But, you know,

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:19.939
there is a constant

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:23.242
fear here of exactly what we may see

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:25.578
in terms of Russian firepower

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.413
focused on frontline towns.

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:28.381
We've seen it ourselves.

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:30.316
I'm hearing sirens around me here

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:31.851
in Aparicio at the moment.

00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:33.019
That have been on all, frankly,

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:34.921
for the past week or so.

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.456
And those evacuations

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:37.790
perhaps heralding

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:38.691
Russia's military,

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:39.559
bracing itself

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:41.828
for a potential Ukrainian onslaught

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:44.063
also Ukrainian officials saying

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:44.597
being used

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:45.431
as cover

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:46.866
to let Russian military

00:07:46.866 --> 00:07:48.668
pull out of some of those towns as well.

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:49.635
So a lot moving

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:51.170
certainly in the northern parts

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.072
of this fringe occupied area.

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:53.806
Julia.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.308
Nick, great to have you with us.

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:57.043
Nick Paton Walsh there. Thank you.

